1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,145
For the exam.

2
00:00:01,145 --> 00:00:06,940
Who is Moyn: a Yale historian of law, critical of the history of human rights.

3
00:00:06,940 --> 00:00:13,072
Status against distributive equality: equal persons, against a limit on the gap.

4
00:00:13,072 --> 00:00:17,044
What the Declaration lacks: any ceiling on inequality.

5
00:00:17,044 --> 00:00:21,002
Croesus: decency beside extreme inequality.

6
00:00:21,002 --> 00:00:28,632
His conclusion: human rights are the wrong tool for inequality; they need a supplement, not a substitute.

